1490-Subpart D—Exclusion of Aliens (for proceedings commenced prior to April 1, 1997)
1491-§ 240.30 Proceedings prior to April 1, 1997. Subpart D of 8 CFR part 240 applies to exclusion proceedings commenced prior to April 1, 1997, pursuant to the former section 236 of the Act. An exclusion proceeding is commenced by the filing of Form I–122 with the Immigration Court, and an alien is considered to be in exclusion proceedings only upon such filing. All references to the Act contained in this subpart are references to the Act in effect prior to April 1, 1997.
1492-§ 240.31 Authority of immigration judges. In determining cases referred for further inquiry as provided in section 235 of the Act, immigration judges shall have the powers and authority conferred upon them by the Act and this chapter. Subject to any specific limitation prescribed by the Act and this chapter, immigration judges shall also exercise the discretion and authority conferred upon the Attorney General by the Act as is appropriate and necessary for the disposition of such cases.
1493-§ 240.32 Hearing. (a) Opening. Exclusion hearings shall be closed to the public, unless the alien at his or her own instance requests that
